         <listPerson>
            <person xml:id="HAU02" sex="1">
               <persName>
                  <roleName>Sir</roleName>
                  <forename>Graves Chamney</forename>
                  <surname>Haughton</surname>
               </persName>
               <birth when="1788"/>
               <death when="1849-08-28"/>
               <occupation>Orientalist</occupation>
               <note type="editorial">
                  <p>Sir Graves Chamney Haughton was an orientalist and honorary secretary of the
                     Royal Asiatic Society, having been a founding member. Haughton was awarded the
                     highest honour of the East India Company, and spent times as a professor in the
                     East India College at Haileybury. He published a number of academic works
                     before his death from cholera whilst in Paris.</p>
                  <p>We distinguish this Haughton from Moses Haughton who was a close friend and associate of henri Fuseli, and appears from 1809 onward.</p>
               </note>
               <bibl type="website">Ed Pope History (03/03/21)</bibl>
               <bibl type="other">DNB</bibl>
            </person>
         </listPerson>
